        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "ff635fee-6e90-522b-adb6-ab4bcea9dcc4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Alexander Glazunov, Marius Petipa\n- Works: Symphony No. 9 in D minor, Raymonda\n- Organizations: Saint Petersburg Conservatory, Petrograd Conservatory, Leningrad Conservatory\n- Events: Bolshevik Revolution\n\nFacts:\n- Alexander Glazunov served as director of the Saint Petersburg Conservatory from 1905 to 1928.\n- Following the Bolshevik Revolution, Alexander Glazunov helped reorganize the Saint Petersburg Conservatory into the Petrograd Conservatory and then the Leningrad Conservatory.\n- Alexander Glazunov began composing Symphony No. 9 in D minor in 1910.\n- Symphony No. 9 in D minor remained unfinished when Alexander Glazunov died in 1936.\n- Raymonda is a ballet in three acts and four scenes with an apotheosis, choreographed by Marius Petipa, with music by Alexander Glazunov, and it is Glazunov's Opus 57.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
